          without permission from Mind Arc Games.
        </p>

        <h2>What Your Account Does Not Give You</h2>

        <p>
          Creating a Mind Arc Network account gives you permission to access and
          use the features we make available to that account. It does not give
          you an ownership interest in Mind Arc Games, the Mind Arc Network, our
          games, our software, or our services.
        </p>

        <p>
          Scores, achievements, rankings, unlocks, cosmetics, virtual items,
          account status, and other game or account features do not represent
          shares, investments, ownership in Mind Arc Games, or a right to Mind
          Arc Games revenue or profits.
        </p>

        <h2>Eligibility</h2>

        <p>
          You must be legally allowed to use our services and create an account
          where you live.
        </p>

        <p>
          If the law where you live requires permission from a parent or legal
          guardian, you must have that permission before using services that
          require it.
        </p>

        <h2>Playing Fair</h2>

        <p>
          We want Mind Arc Games services to be fair, secure, and enjoyable for
          everyone.
        </p>

        <p>You may not:</p>

        <ul>
          <li>Cheat or intentionally exploit bugs or game mechanics.</li>
          <li>
            Use bots, unauthorized scripts, hacks, automation, or other software
            to gain an unfair advantage.
          </li>
          <li>
            Attempt to gain unauthorized access to another person's account, our
            servers, databases, or other systems.
          </li>
          <li>
            Disrupt, damage, attack, or interfere with our games or services.
          </li>
          <li>Impersonate another person.</li>
          <li>
            Use our services for fraud, abuse, or other unlawful activity.
          </li>
        </ul>

        <p>
          Experimenting with a game, discovering a bug, or reporting a security
          problem in good faith is not the same thing as intentionally abusing
          one. If you discover a problem, we encourage you to tell us.
        </p>

        <h2>Our Games and Creative Work</h2>

        <p>
          Mind Arc Games owns, or has permission to use, the games, software,
          artwork, graphics, music, sound effects, logos, trademarks, code,
